BND-16: start a time-series evaporation on the entry in effect at the start date

When the simulation starts between two entries of the [EVAPORATION] TIMESERIES
series, SWMMEngine::initHydrology() moved to the first entry on or after the
start date and used that entry's rate from the start, while during the run each
entry applies from its own date. Move instead to the last entry on or before the
start date and use its rate; setNextEvapDate() then finds the next entry as
before. Same change as the legacy patch. Runs that start on or before the first
entry are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-16_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..ee9b877 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -8851,7 +8851,7 @@ void SWMMEngine::initHydrology() noexcept {
         }
         // legacy climate_initState: NextEvapDate / NextEvapRate. A time-series
         // evaporation starts on its first entry (or, if that lies before the
-        // start date, on the first entry at or after it) and holds each
+        // start date, on the last entry at or before it) and holds each
         // entry's rate until the next entry's date — it is never interpolated.
         {
             auto& cs = ctx_.climate_state;
@@ -8865,8 +8865,13 @@ void SWMMEngine::initHydrology() noexcept {
                     cs.next_evap_date = tbl.x[0];
                     cs.next_evap_rate = tbl.y[0];
                 }
-                if (cs.next_evap_date < ctx_.options.start_date)
-                    setNextEvapDate(ctx_.options.start_date);
+                if (cs.next_evap_date < ctx_.options.start_date) {
+                    while (cs.evap_ts_pos + 1 < static_cast<int>(tbl.x.size()) &&
+                           tbl.x[static_cast<std::size_t>(cs.evap_ts_pos + 1)] <= ctx_.options.start_date)
+                        ++cs.evap_ts_pos;
+                    cs.next_evap_date = tbl.x[static_cast<std::size_t>(cs.evap_ts_pos)];
+                    cs.next_evap_rate = tbl.y[static_cast<std::size_t>(cs.evap_ts_pos)];
+                }
                 cs.evap_rate = cs.next_evap_rate / ucf::UCF(ucf::EVAPRATE, ctx_.options);
                 setNextEvapDate(cs.next_evap_date);
             }
